# petalOS

petalOS is an Android 16 ROM based on LineageOS 23.2. This is the canonical
manifest repository for fetching its source code. petalOS projects are maintained
in the [petalFTW organization](https://github.com/petalFTW).

## Get the source

Use a Linux build host with Git, Git LFS, and the Android `repo` tool installed.
See the [Android build environment requirements](https://source.android.com/docs/setup/start/requirements)
and [source control tools](https://source.android.com/docs/setup/reference/repo)
for host setup.

From an empty source directory, initialize the current development manifest:

```bash
repo init --git-lfs \
  -u https://github.com/petalFTW/manifest.git \
  -b petal-23.2
repo sync -c
```

Git LFS is required for the vendor firmware and application prebuilts. If your
environment sets `GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1`, unset it before syncing so the checkout
contains the binary files rather than LFS pointers.

### Pinned source snapshot

To fetch the source revisions captured on 25 October 2026, use
[`snapshot-20261025.xml`](snapshot-20261025.xml) when initializing an empty source
directory:

```bash
repo init --git-lfs \
  -u https://github.com/petalFTW/manifest.git \
  -b petal-23.2 \
  -m snapshot-20261025.xml
repo sync -c
```

`default.xml` follows the configured development branches. The snapshot pins each
project to a specific commit.

## Build petalOS

The manifest includes these petalOS product configurations:

| Device codename | Product |
| --- | --- |
| `fairlady` | `petal_fairlady` |
| `infiniti` | `petal_infiniti` |
| `macan` | `petal_macan` |
| `macanc` | `petal_macanc` |

From the source root, select the product explicitly. For example, to build
`macanc`:

```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
source vendor/lineage/vars/aosp_target_release
lunch "petal_macanc-${aosp_target_release}-userdebug"
m bacon
```

Replace `petal_macanc` with the product for your device. Using the `petal_` product
selects the petalOS configuration; bare `brunch <codename>` selects the inherited
LineageOS product instead.

## Source layout and upstreams

- `default.xml` defines the platform projects and includes device and ROM snippets.
- `snippets/petal.xml` defines the petalFTW remote and first-party projects.
- The device snippets select device, kernel, and vendor repositories.
- `snapshot-20261025.xml` records the pinned source checkout.

The manifests also fetch unchanged dependencies from LineageOS, AOSP, and other
upstreams. Names such as `LineageOS/*`, `lineage-23.2`, and `vendor/lineage` identify
those dependencies and the inherited build infrastructure. Their original
copyright and license notices remain with the source.
